  "term": "blood pressure",
  "definition": "Blood pressure is a bodily measure that is regulated over time by interacting cardiovascular, kidney, circadian, autonomic, and sleep-wake systems. In a healthy dipping pattern, it falls during the night, whereas a non-dipping pattern means this normal nighttime reduction is reduced or absent.",
